<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Maps and the Map Device (MapDeviceData, MapDeviceManager; settings in config/Custom/MapDevice.ini).

	hideout     where a player arrives in their hideout (.hideout): x, y, z, heading. It is a private copy (instance) of the place.
	            Default: the cabin of the Jinia Guild Hideout, an instance-only room (about 560 x 800).
	  device    where the Map Device stands; its portals open in a ring round it (PortalRadius in the ini).

	difficulty  how many tiers higher a map stronger monsters drop, on top of the tier of their level:
	            champion1/2/3 a Champion of that tier, special a Mage, Thief, Infused, Resonant or wave challenge monster, raid a raid boss.

	strength    how a monster's strength score is worked out (MonsterStrength). Its effective stats (the npc data's, times its passive skills such as
	            "HP Increase (3x)" or "Strong P. Def.") are compared with the standard monster of its level (the lower quartile of each stat over every
	            monster of the level, which is the ordinary monster of that level): 2.0 is twice the standard.
	            The score is the weighted geometric mean of those ratios: 1.0 is an ordinary monster, a Spiked Stakato 2.0, a Maluk Leader 6.1, Knoriks 10.3.
	            The attributes are the weights: hp, pAtk, mAtk, pDef, mDef, pAtkSpd (0 leaves a stat out). HP counts twice, so toughness
	            (HP, P. Def., M. Def.) and offence (P. Atk., M. Atk., Atk. Spd.) weigh about the same. Casting speed is not scored: every npc casts at 333.

	tier        a map tier: tier (1 = lowest), itemId (its "Map (Tier N)" item),
	            minLevel/maxLevel the levels of the monsters of its map, minScore/maxScore their strength score (maxScore 0 = no limit). A map is filled
	            with plain open world monsters that match both (a respawning spawn, they move and give experience: no quest, event or raid monster).
	            If no monster matches, the tier takes the closest in strength of its levels and the server log says so (//mapdevice pool <tier> lists them).
	            dropLevel the lowest monster level that drops this tier; the monster's score must also reach minScore (a monster drops the highest
	            tier both allow, plus its difficulty), so a monster drops the tier it would fill (ordinary monsters never drop the party tiers).
	            hp/attack/defence how much stronger the monsters of its map are, reward the experience, SP and drop chance multiplier of its map.
	            Tiers 1-5 hold solo monsters, tiers 6-10 party monsters: their own strength makes them harder, so their multipliers stay near 1.

	arena       a field a map can open in, picked at random: name, the middle x, y and the ground z, the fence's radiusX/radiusY (an ellipse,
	            at least 500), entryAngle where the players come in (degrees round the middle, 0 = east, 90 = south; the entry is at 80% of the radius).
	            The defaults were checked against the geodata: open, mostly flat ground. A map is its own copy of the place, without its world monsters.

	excludedNpcs monster ids that never fill a map, comma separated.
-->
<list>
	<hideout x="-23560" y="-8963" z="-5384" heading="32768">
		<device x="-23770" y="-8975" z="-5384" heading="0" />
	</hideout>

	<difficulty champion1="0" champion2="1" champion3="2" special="1" raid="2" />

	<strength hp="2" pAtk="1" mAtk="1" pDef="1" mDef="1" pAtkSpd="0.5" />

	<!-- Ordinary monsters, a little stronger every tier. 1: Ketra/Varka, the grazing beasts (0.4-1.0). 2: the Imperial Tomb, the beetles (1.0-1.5). 3: Ragna Orcs, Grave Robbers, the dinosaurs.
	     4: Sel Mahum, Mucrokian, Solina. 5: tough solo monsters: Spiked Stakato, Tanta Lizardmen, Contaminated Batur (1.5-2.6). -->
	<tier tier="1" itemId="50101" minLevel="78" maxLevel="79" minScore="0" maxScore="1.0" dropLevel="78" hp="1.00" attack="1.00" defence="1.00" reward="1.00" />
	<tier tier="2" itemId="50102" minLevel="78" maxLevel="80" minScore="1.0" maxScore="1.5" dropLevel="78" hp="1.05" attack="1.03" defence="1.02" reward="1.10" />
	<tier tier="3" itemId="50103" minLevel="80" maxLevel="82" minScore="0.8" maxScore="1.5" dropLevel="80" hp="1.10" attack="1.05" defence="1.03" reward="1.20" />
	<tier tier="4" itemId="50104" minLevel="82" maxLevel="84" minScore="1.0" maxScore="1.5" dropLevel="82" hp="1.20" attack="1.10" defence="1.05" reward="1.30" />
	<tier tier="5" itemId="50105" minLevel="81" maxLevel="84" minScore="1.5" maxScore="2.6" dropLevel="81" hp="1.10" attack="1.05" defence="1.03" reward="1.45" />
	<!-- Party monsters. 6: Hellbound scouts and mystics, Drake Scout/Mage (2.8-3.7). 7: Drakos, Divinity, Dragon Valley scouts, Hellbound watchers (3.9-5.0).
	     8: Maluks, Dragon Knights, Drake Leader, Tully's Workshop (5.0-6.1). 9: Batwing Drake, Bloody Karik, the Lesser Giants, Hellbound masters (6.6-8.8).
	     10: the Seed of Annihilation elites and Knoriks (10.3-10.6). Their own strength is the step up, so the multipliers stay near 1. -->
	<tier tier="6" itemId="50106" minLevel="82" maxLevel="85" minScore="2.6" maxScore="3.8" dropLevel="82" hp="1.00" attack="1.00" defence="1.00" reward="1.60" />
	<tier tier="7" itemId="50107" minLevel="82" maxLevel="85" minScore="3.8" maxScore="5.0" dropLevel="82" hp="1.00" attack="1.00" defence="1.00" reward="1.80" />
	<tier tier="8" itemId="50108" minLevel="82" maxLevel="85" minScore="5.0" maxScore="6.5" dropLevel="82" hp="1.00" attack="1.00" defence="1.00" reward="2.00" />
	<tier tier="9" itemId="50109" minLevel="82" maxLevel="86" minScore="6.5" maxScore="9.0" dropLevel="82" hp="1.00" attack="1.00" defence="1.00" reward="2.30" />
	<tier tier="10" itemId="50110" minLevel="83" maxLevel="87" minScore="9.0" maxScore="0" dropLevel="85" hp="1.05" attack="1.03" defence="1.02" reward="2.70" />

	<!-- The Team vs Team ring of the Ruins of Despair, drawn a little inside its ring wall. -->
	<arena name="Ruins of Despair" x="-17800" y="142600" z="-3900" radiusX="4800" radiusY="4400" entryAngle="0" />
	<!-- Innadril: the wide bowl of the Field of Whispers. -->
	<arena name="Field of Whispers" x="84000" y="214000" z="-3620" radiusX="4000" radiusY="3500" entryAngle="180" />
	<!-- Aden: the floor of the Silent Valley. -->
	<arena name="Silent Valley" x="172136" y="20325" z="-3328" radiusX="4000" radiusY="4000" entryAngle="90" />
	<!-- Aden: the plain of the Fields of Massacre. -->
	<arena name="Fields of Massacre" x="181000" y="8000" z="-2728" radiusX="3000" radiusY="3000" entryAngle="270" />

	<excludedNpcs></excludedNpcs>
</list>
